:root

*

body

The only difference between Yom Tov and Shabbas is the preparation of food alone,

as it is written: &#8220;Only that which is eaten by every soul &mdash; it alone shall be done for you.&#8221;

Based on the teaching &#8220;Who Is the Man Who Desires Life&#8221;

(Likutay Moharan I, 33; see there, the entire teaching well)

There are two kinds of days: days of good and days of evil, as it is written: &#8220;On a day of good, be in good; and on a day of evil, see&#8221; (Koheles 7:14). Namely, one must look deeply, deeply within the days of evil, and then one will find Hashem, blessed be He, there as well. For &#8220;the whole earth is full of His glory&#8221; (Yeshaya 6:3), and &#8220;there is no place devoid of Him.&#8221; Even in all the languages of the nations and in all the lowest levels, one can find His G-dliness, blessed be He &mdash; for they all receive their vitality from Him, blessed be He, as it is written: &#8220;And You give life to all of them&#8221; (Nechemya 9:6). Only the vitality is in a great tzimtzum [contraction] &mdash; just enough to sustain it. And the tzaddik who conquers his inclination can find His G-dliness, blessed be He, even in the languages of the nations, etc.; see there well.

&darr;

Yom Tov: days of good (no purification) &rarr; but still within time

&darr;

Baking & cooking permitted = reveal the taste = root of delight = love

&darr;

Connect food&#8217;s taste to the light of the love that is in the Daas

&darr;

Airuv tavshilin: don&#8217;t forget that Shabbas is even higher!

&darr;

Shabbas: above time &rarr; light of love in Daas revealed of its own accord &rarr; complete cessation

&#10042; Na Nach Nachma Nachman MayUman &#10042;
